.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: BSD-3-Clause
.Dd November 3, 2026
.Dt MK.LIB.MK 5
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm mk.lib.mk
.Nd library module role: builds, imports or fetches one library
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Fd .include <mk.lib.mk>
.Sh DESCRIPTION
A module directory
.Pa libname.m
or
.Pa name.m
builds one library from
.Pa src/ ,
or takes one from outside with
.Va IMPORT .
Either way, other modules use it the same way, through
.Va LIBS .
Set variables before the
.Ic .include ;
one set after it is not seen.
.Pp
While its own sources compile,
.Dv <LIB>_BUILDING
is defined, in upper case, with anything but letters, digits and underscores
turned into underscores, for the export macros of
.Pa include/bmk_export.h .
.Ss Variables
.Bl -tag -width "IMPORT_HEADERS"
.It Va LIB
The library's base name.
Default: the directory's name without
.Pa .m
and a leading
.Pa lib .
.It Va LIB_SHARED
.Cm YES ,
the default: shared.
.Cm NO :
static only.
.It Va SHLIB_MAJOR
The shared library's major version.
Default 1.
It names
.Pa lib Ns Ar name Ns Pa .so. Ns Ar major
and
.Pa lib Ns Ar name Ns Pa . Ns Ar major Ns Pa .dylib ;
a Windows DLL has no version in its name.
.It Va INCL
Generated headers to make public, by copying them to the framework's
.Pa build/ Ns Ar KEY Ns Pa /include/ .
Others stay private to the module.
.It Va LIBS
Libraries to link.
Link time only: headers come from
.Va PREREQS .
A library's own dependencies are added for you.
.It Va SRCS
Sources, relative to
.Pa src/ .
By default every
.Pa .c , .cc , .cpp , .cxx , .y
and
.Pa .l
file found there, leaving out hidden files.
.It Va LINK_CXX
.Cm yes :
link with
.Va CXX
although the sources are all C, for a module linking a static C++ library.
.It Va REQUIRES
See
.Xr mk.requires.mk 5 .
.It Va PLATFORMS , Va TOOLCHAINS , Va REASON. Ns Ar entry
See
.Xr mk.constraints.mk 5 .
.It Va DELAYLOAD. Ns Ar lib
See
.Xr mk.delayload.mk 5 .
.It Va TESTS_C , Va TESTS_CXX , Va TESTS_SH
See
.Xr mk.test.mk 5 .
.It Va DELAYLOAD
See
.Xr mk.delayload.mk 5 .
.El
.Ss Importing
.Bl -tag -width "IMPORT_HEADERS"
.It Va IMPORT
.Cm pkg: Ns Ar name
from
.Xr pkg-config 1 ,
.Cm prefix: Ns Ar dir
from
.Ar dir Ns Pa /include
and
.Pa lib ,
.Cm fetch: Ns Ar label
a source download, compiled, or
.Cm fetch-bin: Ns Ar label
a prebuilt download.
.It Va IMPORT_HEADERS
Which headers or directories to stage, shell patterns allowed.
Never the whole prefix.
.It Va IMPORT_LIB
.Cm none :
a header-only import, with no library to find.
.It Va IMPORT_PREFIX , Va IMPORT_CFLAGS , Va IMPORT_LIBS
Set in a hook file, these resolve the import before
.Va IMPORT
is looked at.
.It Va FETCH_URL
One or more URLs of the same file, tried in order.
Its checksum must be in the module's
.Pa distinfo .
.It Va FETCH_PATCHES
Files in
.Pa patches/ ,
applied in order with
.Ql patch -p1 .
.It Va FETCH_BUILD
For
.Cm fetch: ,
build with the project's own system instead of
.Va SRCS :
.Cm autotools , cmake , meson
or
.Cm custom .
.It Va FETCH_BUILD_ARGS
Added to the preset's configure step.
.It Va FETCH_BUILD_CMD
With
.Cm custom ,
the command to run, from the source directory, given
.Ev BMK_FETCH_SRCDIR , BMK_FETCH_BUILD_DIR
and
.Ev BMK_FETCH_INSTALL_PREFIX .
.El
.Pp
The first of these that applies resolves an import:
.Bl -enum -offset indent -compact
.It
.Ev <LIB>_PREFIX ,
or
.Ev <LIB>_CFLAGS
with
.Ev <LIB>_LIBS ,
from the environment or command line
.It
.Va IMPORT_PREFIX ,
or
.Va IMPORT_CFLAGS
with
.Va IMPORT_LIBS ,
from a hook file
.It
.Va IMPORT
.It
the prefixes in
.Xr mk.paths 5
.El
.Ss Targets
.Bl -tag -width "copy-up"
.It Cm all
Build or stage into
.Pa build/ Ns Ar KEY Ns Pa /lib/ .
This is the default.
.It Cm copy-up
Build, then copy the library to the framework.
.It Cm test
See
.Xr mk.test.mk 5 .
.It Cm clean
Remove this key's output; with
.Va TARGET=all ,
every key's.
.It Cm help
Print the current selection and the usual variables.
.El
.Pp
On Windows, an imported library's DLL is staged with it whatever its name: the
import library names it, and it is looked for beside that and in
.Pa ../bin .
If it is in neither, the build says which DLL a program will need on
.Ev PATH .
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width "<LIB>_PREFIX"
.It Ev <LIB>_PREFIX
The prefix of an import, with
.Ar LIB
in upper case.
.It Ev PKG_CONFIG_PATH
Searched for
.Cm pkg:
imports.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width "build/KEY/lib/libNAME.linkdeps"
.It Pa src/
sources
.It Pa include/
private headers
.It Pa distinfo
checksums of what
.Va FETCH_URL
names
.It Pa patches/
what
.Va FETCH_PATCHES
names
.It Pa distfiles/ , Pa work/
downloads and their extraction, never committed
.It Pa build/ Ns Ar KEY Ns Pa /lib/
the library
.It Pa build/ Ns Ar KEY Ns Pa /lib/lib Ns Ar name Ns Pa .linkdeps
what a consumer must also link
.It Pa build/ Ns Ar KEY Ns Pa /lib/lib Ns Ar name Ns Pa .delayload
see
.Xr mk.delayload.mk 5
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
A shared library, version 2:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
LIB=geo
SHLIB_MAJOR=2
LIBS=m
\&.include <mk.lib.mk>
.Ed
.Pp
An installed library:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
LIB=png
IMPORT=pkg:libpng
IMPORT_HEADERS=png.h pngconf.h
\&.include <mk.lib.mk>
.Ed
.Pp
A download built with its own CMake:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
LIB=foo
IMPORT=fetch:foo
FETCH_URL=https://example.org/foo-1.0.tar.gz
FETCH_BUILD=cmake
IMPORT_HEADERS=foo.h
\&.include <mk.lib.mk>
.Ed
.Sh DIAGNOSTICS
.Bl -diag
.It IMPORT= Ns Ar value : SRCS= is required
A
.Cm fetch:
source without
.Va FETCH_BUILD
needs its sources named: they are not discovered in a downloaded tree.
.It IMPORT_HEADERS= Ns Ar name : not found under any resolved include dir
The import resolved, and this header is not where it says.
.It IMPORT= Ns Ar value : no library file for Ar lib
No library under the expected names in the resolved directory.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr pkg-config 1 ,
.Xr mk.common.mk 5 ,
.Xr mk.delayload.mk 5 ,
.Xr mk.framework.mk 5 ,
.Xr mk.paths 5 ,
.Xr mk.prog.mk 5 ,
.Xr mk.requires.mk 5 ,
